{
  "_readme": [
    "Every language-specific term the tooling knows, in one place.",
    "",
    "English is the standard's canonical language, but Section 10 says a base may",
    "be authored in ANY language. The scripts used to contradict that: eight",
    "separate tables hardcoded English and Portuguese, so 'any language' really",
    "meant 'either of two, and only by editing Python'.",
    "",
    "TO ADD A LANGUAGE: copy one of the blocks below, translate the values, and",
    "save. Nothing in the code changes. The checker unions the recognition terms",
    "of every language listed here, so it keeps reading a base written in any of",
    "them; the bootstrap writes using exactly one block, chosen by --lang or",
    "detected from the documents themselves.",
    "",
    "Recognition lists are matched lowercased. Include the unaccented spelling",
    "next to the accented one where people realistically type both — EXCEPT for",
    "'status'. Those three values are matched exactly by the Overview's COUNTIF",
    "formulas, so a row spelled 'Em revisao' stops being counted no matter what",
    "this file says. Accepting the variant here would only hide that.",
    "Single strings (spreadsheet_name, uncategorized, ...) are what gets WRITTEN,",
    "so they carry their proper accents and capitalisation."
  ],

